+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering changes to pickup reminders, including switching to email to save the SMS cost.
+Reminders use SMS because an email trial left more pantry orders uncollected and fresh food wasted; volunteers
+have repeatedly proposed the switch without knowing about that trial.
+
+## Reminder behavior
+
+The [reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) sends a member a reminder of their pickup slot the day
+before.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+From April to June 2025, the pantry tried email reminders. As reported in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md),
+the provider's report showed that 34% of reminder emails were never opened. Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13%
+of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag, with its fresh food going in the bin by closing time.
+The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone in the family and never check email, but do see SMS.
+
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025; by August, missed pickups were back to 6%. In the September
+discussion, email was proposed again because SMS cost €40 a month and email was free. The maintainer confirmed
+that pickup reminders would stay on SMS: the saving did not justify the missed pickups and food waste seen
+during the email trial.
